                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "11fcf8d9-519e-3c25-8d7f-bda39528fd36",
                        "entry_id": "4d7e87c4-9be4-3e94-a91e-b0876b97a48a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "an jeden Bürger in einheitlicher Höhe vom Staat ausgezahltes Einkommen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "91dc4706-7dc4-4800-a959-3f04c3bab95e",
                                "sense_id": "11fcf8d9-519e-3c25-8d7f-bda39528fd36",
                                "text": "„Noch vor wenigen Jahren stritten nur ein paar Außenseiter für ein Grundeinkommen, sicher und auskömmlich genug, um den Menschen und den Bürger vom Arbeiter zu emanzipieren. In der breiten Öffentlichkeit fanden sie kaum Gehör. … Heute wird es allenthalben diskutiert …“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aafa323d-37e9-4b1e-b87b-9329743d21d9",
                                "sense_id": "11fcf8d9-519e-3c25-8d7f-bda39528fd36",
                                "text": "Die Parteien sind sich bei der Einführung eines Grundeinkommens noch uneinig."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c648cca-25f7-4954-822b-ded8fa007efb",
                        "source_entry_id": "4d7e87c4-9be4-3e94-a91e-b0876b97a48a",
                        "source_sense_id": "11fcf8d9-519e-3c25-8d7f-bda39528fd36",
                        "source_sense_description": "an jeden Bürger in einheitlicher Höhe vom Staat ausgezahltes Einkommen",
                        "target_lang_word": "basic income",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "basic income",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fcbe3a36-dd24-3d3a-8306-d4f0875e2957",
                                        "entry_id": "52ddd6fd-0f11-3b71-b5b4-b97b937130af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of universal basic income, a form of social security in which all citizens or residents of a jurisdiction receive a sum of money, regularly and unconditionally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c10e075c-e41c-441b-85e9-bb1b8ec152b0",
                                                "sense_id": "fcbe3a36-dd24-3d3a-8306-d4f0875e2957",
                                                "text": "The second feature is the payment by the government of a basic income to all citizens, regardless of their private income or wealth. The amount of basic income should be the same for everyone, and should be calculated to be sufficient to […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8a17884-5126-4ddb-8bbc-5c88cbcbbd9b",
                                                "sense_id": "fcbe3a36-dd24-3d3a-8306-d4f0875e2957",
                                                "text": "The questions to be raised are how processes of globalization, internationalization and economic integration affect national welfare states and what are the consequences for the basic income proposal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7e9ba7f-4772-4525-88e0-d0a708afd930",
                                                "sense_id": "fcbe3a36-dd24-3d3a-8306-d4f0875e2957",
                                                "text": "For example, replacing an existing tax-benefit system with a combination of a basic income and a flat tax such that no income fell below the poverty threshold would presumably result in large changes in many dimensions of behavior which […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e8aebbe-6aea-3676-a571-a9a5b1ca2d20",
                                        "entry_id": "52ddd6fd-0f11-3b71-b5b4-b97b937130af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of guaranteed basic income, a form of social security in which all citizens or residents of a jurisdiction are guaranteed to have an income level at or above the set basic income cut-off level, whereby the government will top-off incomes falling below the line, to reach the limit; those falling above the line would not receive payments."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
